WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:08.000
In the previous lectures, we talked about&nbsp;
predictive modeling pipeline. It involved multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.080
computational steps. In this lecture, we'll focus&nbsp;
on performance evaluation, and what are those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.120
different performance evaluation metrics.
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.200
Predictive model is a function that&nbsp;
map feature x to predict output target&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.400
y. The most common predictive models are either&nbsp;
classification problems or regression problem. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.960
classifications, the target variable y is either&nbsp;
binary or categorical. There are many performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:41.040
metrics associated with classification problems,&nbsp;
such as, true positive rate, false positive rate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.800
positive predictive values, F1 score, area&nbsp;
under the ROC curve, and many, many more.&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.720
&nbsp;
On the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:55.200
if the target variable Y is continuous, we also&nbsp;
have a different performance metrics. Such as mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.040
absolute error, mean squared error, and R squared.&nbsp;
In this lecture, we'll go through all those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:08.480
different performance metrics and explain the&nbsp;
definitions and how they're related to each other.

